WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.753
She didn't forget her cancer appointment.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.484
She couldn't afford the bus fare.

00:00:06.484 --> 00:00:09.571
Would another reminder bring her back?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.139
Meet Setu.

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:20.227
We help cancer care teams understand the reason behind a missed visit, and turn that reason into a practical next step.

00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:24.597
Here is Shanti, nine days overdue.

00:00:24.547 --> 00:00:28.603
The coordinator finds her in a searchable worklist.

00:00:28.603 --> 00:00:34.356
This priority comes from schedule rules, never a clinical risk prediction.

00:00:35.074 --> 00:00:37.957
First, a neutral heads-up.

00:00:37.907 --> 00:00:40.789
Then, an identity check.

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:46.376
Nothing about the missed treatment is disclosed until the patient is verified.

00:00:47.101 --> 00:00:51.387
Her card has expired, and travel is expensive.

00:00:51.337 --> 00:00:59.615
Setu identifies both barriers, surfaces sample support information, and offers an available slot.

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.219
But a booked visit isn't a patient back in care.

00:01:04.169 --> 00:01:07.945
A coordinator confirms attendance separately.

00:01:07.945 --> 00:01:13.213
Now the return is visible, and the activity trail records the action.

00:01:14.037 --> 00:01:18.807
Now, a different reply: weakness and travel cost.

00:01:18.757 --> 00:01:20.913
Watch the difference.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:22.903
Booking stops.

00:01:22.903 --> 00:01:26.717
The patient's exact words go to the nurse queue.

00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:29.956
A person makes the clinical decision.

00:01:30.678 --> 00:01:40.321
The dashboard now tells the story of this session: barriers captured, slots booked, returns confirmed, and reviews still open.

00:01:40.271 --> 00:01:43.256
No invented pilot results.

00:01:43.984 --> 00:01:48.678
Team MedNova pairs a doctor partner with a technical lead.

00:01:48.628 --> 00:01:53.220
This build uses fictional data and simulated calls.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.761
Clinical review and live integrations are the next steps.

00:01:58.496 --> 00:02:00.090
Setu.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.336
A bridge back to care.

00:02:02.336 --> 00:02:05.869
Try the complete journey, with no login.
